# Line endings are part of this repository's product, not a preference.
#
# This repository distributes shell scripts -- `templates/githooks/pre-push`
# and the adapters' hook wrappers -- into other people's checkouts. A `#!/bin/sh`
# script that arrives with CRLF does not run: the interpreter reads the carriage
# return as part of the command and fails with `$'\r': command not found`. Git
# for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file that is the
# ordinary outcome there, not an edge case.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than bare `text=auto`: `text=auto` alone normalises to LF *in
# the repository* but still checks out CRLF on Windows, which is exactly the
# case that breaks. The downstream project that got this right states it the
# same way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
